      ":question/problem": "$\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{-2x^{8}-1}{x^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=$\n\nAssume $x\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{-2x^{8}-1}{x^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int \\left(- 2 x^{6} - \\frac{1}{x^{2}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=-2\\int x^{6}\\,\\mathrm{d}x-\\int x^{-2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=-2\\left(\\frac{x^{7}}{7}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{x^{-1}}{-1}\\right)+C \\\\ &=-\\frac{2x^{7}}{7}+\\frac{1}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
